Wondering actually if we're framing the helper right. Feels unnatural that the dummy password check is done when getting the user and not when checking the password, leading to subtle errors like this (this one was hard to spot). Perhaps the helper can be centered on the password checking step, rather than the user fetching step, for extra explicitness. Something like:

```
def check_password_with_timing_buffer(user, password):
	if user is None:
	    # Run the default password hasher once to reduce the timing
            # difference between an existing and a nonexistent user (#20760).
            UserModel().set_password(password)
     else:
            return user.check_password(password)
```

