reviews.body:
@medmunds I pushed minimal tweaks and I think this is in good shape. If you want to make more changes, just push them, I won't touch the PR until you confirm you are done making edits.

One personal feedback point: while I truly appreciate the granularity of each commit, the review process (making changes and propagating them through the rebase) has been quite painful in practice. I think we can allow ourselves beefier changesets per commit, as long as the changes remain isolated to the same file or conceptual unit.

EDIT: "just push them" I meant

